The value channel: $(goal name) brings a goal up to date, in a fork of this parsed image
as the spawn api runs goals, and answers the goal's value file, trimmed like every
builtin's result. A define for an engine now enters a real rule on that value file,
under $(goal.dir) or .amk/goals, whose recipe writes what the program printed, and the
phony target of the define's name prints it; every $(goal x) in the body is a
prerequisite on x's value file, so referencing a value declares the edge and the cell
reruns only when a value it reads is newer. A plain file target's value is the file
itself, copied into the value directory by a pattern rule the first define enters.

